        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A black concrete driveway is entirely achievable, and on the right house it looks excellent. The decision that matters is where the colour lives. Integral colour and stain put it in the concrete, where it lasts and wears gracefully; tinted sealers and paints put it in a film, where it is blacker and more even but wears in the lanes and needs renewing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most existing driveways the best balance is a black water-based stain under a driveway-rated sealer, maintained by resealing when the water test says so. For a new pour, use black iron oxide in the mix and finish over it. Either way, budget for the sealer before you budget for the colour, because the sealer is what keeps it black.
          </p>
        </div>

